  "index": 4,
  "response": " This text is a speech given by Pope Urban II at the Council of Clermont in 1095 CE, which called for the First Crusade. The Pope describes the plight of Christian lands, particularly Jerusalem and Constantinople, allegedly under attack by non-Christian Persians who have destroyed churches, enslaved or killed Christians, and dismantled the Greek kingdom. He urges European nations, especially those with a history of military prowess, to avenge these wrongs and recover the lost territory. The Pope mentions the past glory of Charlemagne and other kings who extended Christian territory and cites the desecration of the Holy Sepulchre as a specific reason for action. He encourages European armies to embark on this journey as a way to redeem their sins, promising the promise of eternal glory in heaven.",
